WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.009 --> 00:00:01.724
- K thanks, bye.

00:00:01.724 --> 00:00:04.307
(upbeat music)

00:00:06.516 --> 00:00:08.561
- It's kinda sad but my
relationship with my phone

00:00:08.561 --> 00:00:11.159
is my longest, most intimate relationship.

00:00:11.159 --> 00:00:14.089
- Everybody who knows me
they know what's going on

00:00:14.089 --> 00:00:15.290
in my life all the time

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:18.318
because I'm always on Snapchat
Stories or Instagram Stories.

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:21.160
- Pretty much anything I do
on my phone is a waste of time

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:22.821
unless I am doing something for work.

00:00:22.821 --> 00:00:25.244
I have little to no idea
what I will be doing

00:00:25.244 --> 00:00:27.682
except for the fact that
it involves my phone

00:00:27.682 --> 00:00:30.075
and kind of going off
the grid a little bit?

00:00:30.075 --> 00:00:30.908
- Okay...

00:00:32.224 --> 00:00:34.256
Am I gonna get it back? (laughs)

00:00:34.256 --> 00:00:35.089
Oh my God!

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:37.192
No!

00:00:37.192 --> 00:00:38.025
- No.

00:00:39.721 --> 00:00:42.586
- Oh no, this is the
phone my grandmother has.

00:00:42.586 --> 00:00:43.757
- I do like the look.

00:00:43.757 --> 00:00:46.646
But like functionally what am
I supposed to do with this?

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:50.396
- Okay, am I supposed
to use this for a week?

00:00:51.273 --> 00:00:52.511
Oh no! (laughs)

00:00:52.511 --> 00:00:54.344
- Oh, it has a camera!

00:00:56.428 --> 00:00:58.939
- This is where I say, "I
love you guys, wish me luck,

00:00:58.939 --> 00:01:01.022
and hopefully I survive."

00:01:01.919 --> 00:01:05.175
You can have it, I can't
look at it anymore.

00:01:05.175 --> 00:01:07.675
- One last selfie before I go.

00:01:09.938 --> 00:01:11.328
- It's the first official day.

00:01:11.328 --> 00:01:13.238
I'm taking this challenge very seriously.

00:01:13.238 --> 00:01:15.647
- Someone over here
doesn't know how to turn on

00:01:15.647 --> 00:01:16.811
her own phone
- I don't know

00:01:16.811 --> 00:01:17.801
- [Rafa] How to turn my phone on (laughs)

00:01:17.801 --> 00:01:19.103
- Look at the era we live in,

00:01:19.103 --> 00:01:21.079
these privileged Millennials these days.

00:01:21.079 --> 00:01:24.264
- You know the home screen
that we have on our iPhones?

00:01:24.264 --> 00:01:26.374
This doesn't have that so
I don't know what to press.

00:01:26.374 --> 00:01:28.490
- I am currently in the bathroom.

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:31.038
I have to go old school.

00:01:31.038 --> 00:01:34.398
- I have to go to Staples but
I don't know where Staples is

00:01:34.398 --> 00:01:36.589
so I had to print out
Google Maps. (laughs)

00:01:36.589 --> 00:01:37.995
- Okay, first comes first,

00:01:37.995 --> 00:01:40.519
learning how to fold a freaking map.

00:01:40.519 --> 00:01:42.112
Help me!

00:01:42.112 --> 00:01:44.993
So I added my parents as
contacts for the first time today

00:01:44.993 --> 00:01:46.816
and it was struggle texting them.

00:01:46.816 --> 00:01:49.234
Instead of hitting the space
bar which I was trying to find,

00:01:49.234 --> 00:01:50.293
I hit send.

00:01:50.293 --> 00:01:52.215
It literally says this

00:01:52.215 --> 00:01:54.320
- I would go back to flip
phones, to be honest.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:57.050
I feel like life was just a simpler time

00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:00.662
We appreciated more
when we had flip phones.

00:02:00.662 --> 00:02:02.396
- [Liz] Yeah, that's pretty good.

00:02:02.396 --> 00:02:03.402
Okay!

00:02:03.402 --> 00:02:06.402
- I'd put that on my Tinder profile.

00:02:08.686 --> 00:02:10.302
- I actually had to ask my coworkers

00:02:10.302 --> 00:02:13.139
what they did over this
past weekend and likewise,

00:02:13.139 --> 00:02:16.651
they had no visibility into
what my weekend looked like,

00:02:16.651 --> 00:02:18.851
so now I'm super mysterious.

00:02:18.851 --> 00:02:21.684
- So the alarm on this stupid
flip phone did not go off.

00:02:21.684 --> 00:02:26.199
It's now 9:30 and I'm supposed
to be at work at 9:30 so...

00:02:26.199 --> 00:02:28.949
(subway chatter)

00:02:32.574 --> 00:02:34.147
- I haven't charged all week, by the way,

00:02:34.147 --> 00:02:36.177
and it's still alive somehow?

00:02:36.177 --> 00:02:39.003
Now I realize how much battery
smartphones actually drain.

00:02:39.003 --> 00:02:41.623
As long as I have something
to tell me the time

00:02:41.623 --> 00:02:44.206
and something to tell me when
the train comes, I am good.

00:02:44.206 --> 00:02:45.039
- Oh...

00:02:46.341 --> 00:02:51.191
I am looking at PornHub.com
on a flip phone right now.

00:02:51.191 --> 00:02:54.259
And it's a horrible user experience.

00:02:54.259 --> 00:02:56.054
Yeah, I'm gonna have
to go offline for this.

00:02:56.054 --> 00:02:59.513
- I'm becoming very
irritable very quickly.

00:02:59.513 --> 00:03:01.031
It is really hindering my work

00:03:01.031 --> 00:03:04.523
because I can't get my
emails, get my Slack messages.

00:03:04.523 --> 00:03:05.856
- I miss emojis.

00:03:06.874 --> 00:03:08.541
This is my life now.

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:13.571
- So we're just gonna wander
around the streets of New York

00:03:13.571 --> 00:03:14.601
while it's raining.

00:03:14.601 --> 00:03:16.531
Can I just look at your GPS?

00:03:16.531 --> 00:03:17.501
Am I allowed to do that?

00:03:17.501 --> 00:03:20.873
- Over the past few days I've
been a lot more productive

00:03:20.873 --> 00:03:22.835
than I've been in a very long time

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:24.263
because I'm not texting here

00:03:24.263 --> 00:03:26.603
and checking in with apps there.

00:03:26.603 --> 00:03:28.034
- Today is Fri-yay,

00:03:28.034 --> 00:03:32.201
or the last day that I'm
doing this stupid challenge.

00:03:33.554 --> 00:03:34.387
Menu?

00:03:35.744 --> 00:03:37.917
- I am vlogging from Hawaii today.

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:39.690
After a week of no iPhone

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:43.443
I feel like I'm getting
back from a little mini vaca

00:03:43.443 --> 00:03:45.333
so I thought this was appropriate.

00:03:45.333 --> 00:03:48.583
- Learned a trick with my phone, watch!

00:03:50.252 --> 00:03:52.337
- At this point I've
gotten pretty frickin' good

00:03:52.337 --> 00:03:54.624
at living life without an iPhone.

00:03:54.624 --> 00:03:57.291
I've even figured out some hacks

00:03:58.851 --> 00:04:00.132
with my flip phone.

00:04:00.132 --> 00:04:02.622
- I'm going to treat
myself to a nice dinner,

00:04:02.622 --> 00:04:05.391
and I think I might go
tech free for dinner.

00:04:05.391 --> 00:04:09.570
Might just leave everything
including the stupid flip phone.

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:11.492
- You would think it's really dramatic

00:04:11.492 --> 00:04:12.868
but it's classical addiction,

00:04:12.868 --> 00:04:15.239
where you think you can't
live without something

00:04:15.239 --> 00:04:17.201
and then you're like "I'm
fine, the world is fine,

00:04:17.201 --> 00:04:19.488
they don't need my InstaStories
and I don't need theirs."

00:04:19.488 --> 00:04:21.020
- The main thing that I noticed was

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:24.591
I was just keeping my head up
more and I was looking around

00:04:24.591 --> 00:04:26.881
and noticing things I
hadn't noticed before.

00:04:26.881 --> 00:04:29.473
I read parts of a couple different books.

00:04:29.473 --> 00:04:31.262
- But it was just mainly
giving up social media

00:04:31.262 --> 00:04:33.092
that was kind of a struggle,

00:04:33.092 --> 00:04:34.662
especially because I did go out a lot.

00:04:34.662 --> 00:04:36.262
Oh my God, that's actually really cool.

00:04:36.262 --> 00:04:37.841
- Right?

00:04:37.841 --> 00:04:39.324
- [Rafa] Thank you Jade, I love you!

00:04:39.324 --> 00:04:42.427
Also I had to carry around a
map of Manhattan in my purse.

00:04:42.427 --> 00:04:45.599
- If anything this has made
me more reliant on my iPhone

00:04:45.599 --> 00:04:49.602
because I felt like a
part of me was missing.

00:04:49.602 --> 00:04:53.600
I wasn't so easily accessible
and people couldn't reach me.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:56.703
- I was just a lot more present
in everything that I did.

00:04:56.703 --> 00:04:59.197
And I've never been so focused.

00:04:59.197 --> 00:05:00.837
- Sometimes you've just
gotta live in the moment.

00:05:00.837 --> 00:05:02.573
It's better you liking your own life

00:05:02.573 --> 00:05:04.503
than posting on social media

00:05:04.503 --> 00:05:06.474
and having other people envy yours.

00:05:06.474 --> 00:05:09.522
- I just feel like I'm in a
better mental, spiritual place.

00:05:09.522 --> 00:05:12.124
- My last words to this flip phone are

00:05:12.124 --> 00:05:14.490
(phone click)

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:16.420
- I'm ready to be reunited with my iPhone.

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:17.253
- My baby!

00:05:19.593 --> 00:05:22.696
- Feels good to have
this back in my hands.

00:05:22.696 --> 00:05:26.382
It feels good and I feel
like a complete person again.

00:05:26.382 --> 00:05:28.294
I'm gonna go take a bunch of selfies.

00:05:28.294 --> 00:05:30.877
(techno music)

